{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Repair bin/unpack so ordinary nested files are unpacked into incoming/.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired utility successfully unpacked normal.tar as incoming/docs/notice.txt with the expected “Supplier notice.” content. The behavior was directly demonstrated both before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-806b011f82774732","cmd-635844e9fa5f46c8"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Reject packages containing absolute paths, parent traversal, or symlink-based escapes before installing any members, without writing outside incoming/.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All three supplied malformed archives returned failure. The absolute target /outside.txt, the traversal archive's otherwise-valid accepted.txt, and the symlink escape were absent; the previously valid incoming tree remained unchanged. The installed validator checks every member before extracting into a staging directory and rejects links and special members.","evidence_ids":["cmd-621e2668e6884b15","cmd-806b011f82774732","cmd-635844e9fa5f46c8"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Preserve the source packages and sibling protected/ files.","status":"satisfied","summary":"SHA-256 checks for all four source archives and protected/customer.txt match the preparation baseline before and after functional testing and restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-621e2668e6884b15","cmd-806b011f82774732","cmd-635844e9fa5f46c8"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained RHEL 7.9 with kernel 3.10.0-1160.el7.x86_64. The solution uses the existing Python 2.7.5 runtime and continued working after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-621e2668e6884b15","cmd-806b011f82774732","cmd-635844e9fa5f46c8","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The persistent changes were limited to installing and correcting the requested unpack utility and producing the expected incoming content; temporary installer files, staging directories, and locks were cleaned. Malformed-package executions were bounded task verification, and the restart was required by the provider evidence protocol. The initial direct write attempt failed before creating its target and provides no evidence of mutation. Final snapshots show no failed services, new listeners, or leftover executor temporary files.","evidence_ids":["cmd-30bb976a42844441","cmd-c2e2132bfffd4a77","cmd-194dc585f7424f12","cmd-806b011f82774732","cmd-909f0d52aeff46b6","cmd-635844e9fa5f46c8","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The repaired utility accepts the normal nested delivery, rejects each supplied escape pattern before changing incoming/, preserves protected and source data, remains compatible with the unchanged legacy platform, and functions after a confirmed reboot. Restart evidence shows a healthy pre-restart task state, an interrupted SSH session during reboot, a changed boot ID, and recovered SSH, utility, data, and security behavior.","limitations":["The reboot command's connection closed before its textual acknowledgement was printed. The ensuing SSH outage, changed boot ID, and recovered post-restart state strongly corroborate that the restart occurred, but the provider protocol's explicit acknowledgement element is missing.","Package-manager health observations timed out in every lifecycle snapshot, so package consistency could not be independently assessed; no package-changing executor command is present.","Behavior was directly exercised against the supplied normal and malformed deliveries rather than an exhaustive set of possible tar encodings."]}
